IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `saeo-dates`
IMPORT `saeo-rules`

-- Equal Opportunity Act 1984 (SA) -- the questions of the COMPLAINANT.
--
-- SEAT: the person who is discriminated against, sexually harassed or victimised at work or in seeking work (a job
-- applicant, an employee or unpaid worker, a commission agent, an independent contractor, a contract worker, a partner),
-- and who complains about it to the Commissioner for Equal Opportunity and takes it on to SAET or the Tribunal. "Was I
-- discriminated against?", "Is it unlawful, or does an exemption cover it?", "Was it sexual harassment?", "Was I
-- victimised?", "Is my employer liable too?", "Can I complain, and by when?", "Where will it be heard, and what can be
-- ordered?", "Can I appeal?", "Does an unfair dismissal claim shut this one out?". The employer, the principal, the
-- Commissioner, SAET, the Tribunal and the Supreme Court get no seat: their judgments and findings are asked as facts.
--
-- Every question takes plain facts (yes/no, dates, a choice from a list) and calls the rules of saeo-rules.l4. The time
-- limits are DEONTIC rules run inside the questions that ask whether a step was in time; no question takes a DEONTIC or
-- an EVENT.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Based on content from the South Australian Legislation website at 6 November 2026 (c) State of South
-- Australia, CC BY 4.0; not the authorised version. See SOURCE-LICENSE.md. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as
-- advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Equal Opportunity Act 1984 (SA): the complainant's questions`

§§ `Where I stand: the grounds`

@export Is my condition a "disability" under the Equal Opportunity Act 1984 (SA) s 5(1)? It is if it is a total or partial loss of bodily or mental functions or of a part of the body, organisms in the body causing (or capable of causing) disease or illness, a malfunction, malformation or disfigurement of part of the body, a disorder that makes you learn differently, or a disorder, illness or disease affecting thought, perception, emotions or judgment or causing disturbed behaviour. A past disability, or one that may exist in the future, counts too (s 66(a)).
GIVEN `which describes my condition` IS A `Condition` @desc Which of the Act's descriptions fits your condition. One of: "total or partial loss of bodily or mental functions", "total or partial loss of a part of the body", "organisms in the body causing disease or illness", "organisms in the body capable of causing disease or illness", "malfunction, malformation or disfigurement of a part of the body", "a disorder or malfunction that makes me learn differently", "a disorder, illness or disease affecting thought, perception, emotions or judgment, or causing disturbed behaviour", "none of these"
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is my condition a disability` MEANS
    `s 5 -- it is a disability` `which describes my condition`

@export Do I have "caring responsibilities" under the Equal Opportunity Act 1984 (SA) s 5(3)? You do if you care for or support your dependent child (including an adopted, step- or ex-nuptial child who is wholly or substantially dependent on you), or another immediate family member (a spouse or domestic partner, current or former; an adult child, parent, grandparent, grandchild or sibling of yours or your partner's) who needs care and support; and, for an Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander person, anyone related to you under kinship rules.
GIVEN `whom do I care for or support` IS A `Whom I care for` @desc Whom you care for or support. One of: "my child who is wholly or substantially dependent on me", "my spouse or domestic partner, or former spouse or domestic partner", "an adult child, parent, grandparent, grandchild or sibling of mine or of my spouse or domestic partner", "another relative", "a person related to me by Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander kinship rules", "no one"
      `do they need care and support` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that family member is in need of care and support (not asked for a dependent child)
      `am I Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander person
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Do I have caring responsibilities` MEANS
    `s 5(3) -- I have caring responsibilities` `whom do I care for or support` `do they need care and support` `am I Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander`

§§ `Was I discriminated against`

@export Did they discriminate against me on this ground, as the Equal Opportunity Act 1984 (SA) defines it (ss 6, 29, 51, 66, 85A, 85T)? They did if they treated you less favourably than they treat (or would treat) someone without the attribute, and the attribute was at least a substantial reason -- directly; or because you cannot meet a requirement that a substantially higher proportion of people without the attribute can meet and that is not reasonable; or because of a characteristic generally of (or imputed to) people with the attribute; or because of the attribute of a relative or associate. Some grounds add ways (disability: access, special assistance or equipment, an assistance animal; gender identity: being required to take on characteristics of a sex you do not identify with; religious dress: being required to alter it) and some have fewer. It is still discrimination if they were mistaken about you (s 6(4)).
GIVEN `the ground` IS A `Ground` @desc The ground. One of: "sex", "gender identity", "sexual orientation", "intersex status", "race" (nationality, country of origin, colour or ancestry), "disability", "age", "marital or domestic partnership status", "identity of my spouse or domestic partner", "pregnancy" (including potential pregnancy), "association with a child" (breast or bottle feeding, or being accompanied by a child), "caring responsibilities", "religious appearance or dress", "being subjected to domestic abuse"
      `how was it done` IS A `How it was done` @desc How it was done. One of: "treating me unfavourably because of the attribute", "treating me unfavourably because I cannot comply with a requirement", "treating me unfavourably because of a characteristic of people with the attribute", "treating me unfavourably because of the attribute of a relative or associate", "requiring me to assume characteristics of a sex I do not identify with", "requiring me to alter my religious appearance or dress", "failing to provide safe and proper access to a place or facilities I need because of my disability", "treating me unfavourably because I need special access to a place or facilities", "failing to provide special assistance or equipment I need because of my disability", "treating me unfavourably because I need special assistance or equipment", "treating me unfavourably because of my assistance animal"
      `was I treated less favourably than someone without the attribute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they treated you less favourably than, in the same or similar circumstances, they treat or would treat someone without the attribute
      `was the ground at least a substantial reason` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the attribute (or your not meeting the requirement, or your need) was at least a substantial reason for what they did, even if there were other reasons
      `can a substantially higher proportion of others comply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a requirement: whether a substantially higher proportion of people without the attribute comply, or can comply, with it
      `is the requirement unreasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a requirement: whether the requirement is not reasonable in the circumstances (a judgment for the Tribunal or SAET)
      `were they able to provide the access` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For access to a place or facilities: whether they were able to bring about the access or use
      `was it unreasonable not to provide it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For special assistance or equipment: whether it was unreasonable in the circumstances to fail to provide it, or to treat you unfavourably for needing it
      `is it an assistance animal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an animal: whether it is an assistance animal (an accredited assistance dog under the Dog and Cat Management Act 1995, or a prescribed class)
      `is the appearance or dress religious` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For religious appearance or dress: whether it is required by, or symbolic of, your (or your relative's or associate's) religious beliefs
      `am I pregnant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For pregnancy: whether you are pregnant now (a requirement or a characteristic is covered only for a pregnant woman; potential pregnancy is covered for direct treatment)
      `am I the perpetrator of the abuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For domestic abuse through a relative or associate: whether you are yourself the perpetrator of the domestic abuse
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Was I discriminated against on this ground` MEANS
    `ss 6, 29, 51, 66, 85A, 85T -- they discriminated against me` `the ground` `how was it done` (`Treatment facts` WITH
        `less favourably than a person without the attribute` IS `was I treated less favourably than someone without the attribute`
        `the ground was at least a substantial reason` IS `was the ground at least a substantial reason`
        `a substantially higher proportion without the attribute can comply` IS `can a substantially higher proportion of others comply`
        `the requirement is not reasonable in the circumstances` IS `is the requirement unreasonable`
        `they were able to effect the access` IS `were they able to provide the access`
        `it was unreasonable in the circumstances` IS `was it unreasonable not to provide it`
        `the animal is an assistance animal` IS `is it an assistance animal`
        `the appearance or dress is required by or symbolic of religious beliefs` IS `is the appearance or dress religious`
        `I am pregnant` IS `am I pregnant`
        `I am the perpetrator of the domestic abuse` IS `am I the perpetrator of the abuse`)

§§ `Is it unlawful at work`

@export Does the religious school exemption cover the discrimination in my job (Equal Opportunity Act 1984 (SA) ss 34(3), 85Z(2))? A religious educational institution may discriminate in employment or engagement on the ground of sexual orientation, gender identity or intersex status (and marital or domestic partnership status against same sex domestic partners) only if the discrimination is founded on the religion's precepts and it has a written policy stating its position, gave you a copy before interview or offer, and provides it free on request.
GIVEN `which ground` IS A `Ground` @desc The ground of the discrimination (see the discrimination question for the choices)
      `am I in a same sex domestic partnership` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are one of a same sex couple of domestic partners
      `is the work for an educational institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employment or engagement is for the purposes of an educational institution (a school, college, university or other place of education or training)
      `is it run on the precepts of a religion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the institution is administered in accordance with the precepts of a particular religion
      `is the discrimination founded on those precepts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the discrimination is founded on the precepts of that religion
      `does it have a written policy on it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the educational authority has a written policy stating its position on the matter
      `was I given a copy before interview or offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were given a copy of the policy before being interviewed for, or offered, the employment or engagement
      `is the policy given free on request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a copy of the policy is provided free of charge on request to staff, contractors, students, parents and the public
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does the religious school exemption cover my job` MEANS
    `ss 34(3), 85Z(2) -- the religious school exemption applies` `which ground` `am I in a same sex domestic partnership` `is the work for an educational institution` `is it run on the precepts of a religion` `is the discrimination founded on those precepts` `does it have a written policy on it` `was I given a copy before interview or offer` `is the policy given free on request`

@export Does the pregnancy exemption cover what was done to me (Equal Opportunity Act 1984 (SA) s 85Z(3))? Discrimination against a pregnant woman at work is not unlawful if it is based on her being unable to do the work genuinely and reasonably required without endangering herself, the unborn child or others, or to respond to foreseeable emergencies; and, if she was dismissed, only if there was no other work the employer could reasonably be expected to offer and she declined leave offered for the period.
GIVEN `am I pregnant now` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are (or were at the time) pregnant
      `was it because I could not safely do the work or respond to emergencies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether what was done was based on your not being able to do the work genuinely and reasonably required of you without endangering yourself, the unborn child or others, or to respond to reasonably foreseeable emergencies
      `was I dismissed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether what was done was to dismiss you
      `was there no other work for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a dismissal: whether there was no other work the employer could reasonably be expected to offer you
      `did I decline leave offered for the period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a dismissal: whether you were offered leave for the period you would be unable to do the work, and declined it
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does the pregnancy exemption cover it` MEANS
    `s 85Z(3) -- the pregnancy exemption applies` `am I pregnant now` `was it because I could not safely do the work or respond to emergencies` `was I dismissed` `was there no other work for me` `did I decline leave offered for the period`

@export Is the discrimination against me at work unlawful under the Equal Opportunity Act 1984 (SA) (Part 3 Division 2 ss 30-34, Part 4 Division 2 ss 52-56, Part 5 Division 2 ss 67-71, Part 5A Division 2 ss 85B-85F, Part 5B Division 2 ss 85U-85Z, with each Part's general exemptions)? It is unlawful for an employer, principal or firm to discriminate against a job applicant, employee, commission agent, independent contractor, contract worker or partner (or one seeking such a position) in deciding who gets the position, the terms offered, the terms of the work, access to promotion, transfer, training or other benefits, dismissal or ending the engagement, or any other detriment -- unless the work is for purposes not connected with their business (employees and independent contractors), or an exemption that reaches the ground applies. Discrimination because you are breast feeding or accompanied by a child is not covered by the work Division (s 85U).
GIVEN `the ground of it` IS A `Ground` @desc The ground (see the discrimination question for the choices)
      `my position` IS A `My position` @desc Your position. One of: "someone applying for employment", "an employee" (including an unpaid worker, or the holder of a public or statutory office that is not judicial), "someone seeking engagement as a commission agent", "a commission agent", "someone seeking engagement as an independent contractor", "an independent contractor", "a contract worker" (working for a principal while employed or engaged by someone else, as in labour hire), "someone seeking to become a partner", "a partner", "none of these"
      `what did they do` IS A `What was done` @desc What they did. One of: "deciding who should be offered the position", "the terms or conditions on which the position was offered", "the terms or conditions of my work or membership", "denying or limiting access to promotion, transfer, training or other benefits", "dismissing me, ending my engagement or expelling me", "not allowing me to work" (contract worker), "a contract or arrangement under which I am to be discriminated against" (contract worker), "subjecting me to other detriment" (including humiliation, denigration, or segregation from people of other races)
      `did they discriminate against me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they discriminated against you on that ground (see the discrimination question)
      `is the work not connected with their business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer employs you, or the principal engages you as an independent contractor, for purposes not connected with a business they carry on (for example a nanny or gardener in their home)
      `which exemption do they rely on` IS AN `Exemption` @desc The exemption they rely on. One of: "none", "a genuine occupational requirement", "a religious educational institution", "standards of appearance and dress reasonably required", "I cannot do the work genuinely and reasonably required, or respond to emergencies", "complying with an industrial award or agreement", "a youth rate of pay under an award or agreement", "a measure intended to achieve equality", "a project for the benefit of people of a particular race, disability or age", "a body established for religious purposes", "a charitable instrument", "rates of pay for people with disabilities", "preventing the spread of an infectious disease", "unjustifiable hardship in providing access to a place or facilities" (s 84: only where it is about access to or use of a place or facilities), "rights or privileges for women in connection with pregnancy or childbirth", "confidentiality, conflicts of interest, nepotism, or health and safety", "refusing to reveal my face for identity verification", "caring for a child where the child lives", "an exemption granted by the Tribunal"
      `are its conditions met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the facts meet that exemption's conditions (for the religious school and pregnancy exemptions, see those questions; for the others, as the Tribunal or SAET would find; for unjustifiable hardship, that the discrimination concerns access to or use of a place or facilities and that providing it would impose unjustifiable hardship, weighing the benefit or detriment to those concerned, the effect of your disability, and their finances and the cost (s 84(2)))
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is the discrimination against me at work unlawful` MEANS
    `Part 3-5B Division 2 -- the discrimination at work is unlawful` `the ground of it` `my position` `what did they do` `did they discriminate against me` `is the work not connected with their business` `which exemption do they rely on` `are its conditions met`

@export Is the compulsory retirement term in my award or agreement void (Equal Opportunity Act 1984 (SA) s 85EA)? A provision of an award, determination or agreement made or approved under the Fair Work Act 1994 (SA) that imposes, requires or authorises a compulsory retiring age, or requires or authorises termination because of age, is void and of no effect.
GIVEN `is it in a State award or agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the provision is in an industrial or enterprise award, determination or agreement made or approved under the Fair Work Act 1994 (SA) (not a Commonwealth award or agreement)
      `does it set a retiring age or termination for age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the provision imposes (or requires or authorises the employer to impose) a compulsory retiring age, or requires or authorises termination of employment because of age
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is the compulsory retirement term void` MEANS
    `s 85EA -- the provision is void` `is it in a State award or agreement` `does it set a retiring age or termination for age`

§§ `Sexual harassment (only if you were sexually harassed)`

@export Was what happened to me "sexual harassment" under the Equal Opportunity Act 1984 (SA) s 87(9)? It was if the person made an unwelcome sexual advance or an unwelcome request for sexual favours, or engaged in other unwelcome conduct of a sexual nature (including a sexual statement made to you or in your presence, orally or in writing), in circumstances in which a reasonable person would have anticipated that you would be offended, humiliated or intimidated.
GIVEN `what was the conduct` IS A `The conduct` @desc What the person did. One of: "an unwelcome sexual advance", "an unwelcome request for sexual favours", "other unwelcome conduct of a sexual nature, including a sexual statement", "none of these"
      `would a reasonable person have expected me to be offended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a reasonable person, having regard to all the circumstances, would have anticipated that you would be offended, humiliated or intimidated
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Was it sexual harassment` MEANS
    `s 87(9) -- it was sexual harassment` `what was the conduct` `would a reasonable person have expected me to be offended`

@export Was the sexual harassment by someone I work with unlawful (Equal Opportunity Act 1984 (SA) s 87(1))? It is unlawful to sexually harass a person you work with (both carry out duties, paid or not, in or for the same business or organisation) or someone seeking to become a fellow worker, while at a place that is a workplace of both of you, or in circumstances where the harasser knew or ought reasonably to have known you were (or were seeking to be) a fellow worker.
GIVEN `was it sexual harassment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was sexual harassment (see that question)
      `how are we connected at work` IS A `How we are connected at work` @desc Your connection with the harasser. One of: "we carry out duties for the same business or organisation", "I was seeking to become their fellow worker", "neither"
      `was it at a workplace of us both` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it happened at a place (including a ship, aircraft or vehicle) where both of you work or attend in connection with your work
      `did they know or should they have known` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the harasser was, or ought reasonably to have been, aware that you were a fellow worker or seeking to become one
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Was the sexual harassment at work unlawful` MEANS
    `s 87(1) -- the sexual harassment at work was unlawful` `was it sexual harassment` `how are we connected at work` `was it at a workplace of us both` `did they know or should they have known`

@export Was my employer's failure to stop further sexual harassment by a customer, client or other outsider unlawful (Equal Opportunity Act 1984 (SA) s 87(7))? If you reported to your employer specific circumstances in which you were sexually harassed at work by someone who is not a fellow worker, and it is reasonable to expect that person to do it again, it is unlawful for the employer to fail to take reasonable steps to prevent it.
GIVEN `was I harassed at work by an outsider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were sexually harassed, in the course of your employment, by a person who is not a fellow worker (for example a customer, client or patient)
      `did I report the specific circumstances to my employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you reported the specific circumstances to your employer
      `is it reasonable to expect it to happen again` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is reasonable in all the circumstances to expect further sexual harassment of you by the same person
      `did my employer take reasonable steps to prevent it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer took reasonable steps to prevent the further harassment
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Was my employer's failure to protect me unlawful` MEANS
    `s 87(7) -- my employer's failure to prevent further harassment is unlawful` `was I harassed at work by an outsider` `did I report the specific circumstances to my employer` `is it reasonable to expect it to happen again` `did my employer take reasonable steps to prevent it`

§§ `Victimisation (only if you were treated badly for using the Act)`

@export Was I victimised (Equal Opportunity Act 1984 (SA) s 86)? It is unlawful to treat you unfavourably on the ground that you brought proceedings, gave evidence or information, made allegations of a contravention, reasonably asserted a right to complain, or did anything else under or by reference to the Act -- or because they knew you intended to, or suspected you had or would. Treating you unfavourably because an allegation was false, or because you did not act in good faith, is not victimisation.
GIVEN `what did I do` IS A `What I did under the Act` @desc What you did, intended to do, or were suspected of having done or intending. One of: "brought proceedings under the Act", "gave evidence or information in proceedings under the Act", "made allegations of a contravention of the Act", "asserted a right to complain or take proceedings under the Act", "did something else under or by reference to the Act", "none of these"
      `was my assertion reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For asserting a right: whether the assertion was reasonable
      `was I treated less favourably for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they treated you less favourably than they treat, or would treat, someone who had not done it
      `was it at least a substantial reason` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether what you did (or their knowledge or suspicion of it) was at least a substantial reason for the treatment
      `was my allegation false` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the allegation you made was false
      `did I act in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you acted in good faith
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Was I victimised` MEANS
    `s 86 -- I was victimised` `what did I do` `was my assertion reasonable` `was I treated less favourably for it` `was it at least a substantial reason` `was my allegation false` `did I act in good faith`

§§ `Who is liable`

@export Is the employer or principal liable for what its employee or agent did to me (Equal Opportunity Act 1984 (SA) s 91)? A person is vicariously liable for a discriminatory or unlawful act of its employee or agent done in the course of the employment or agency, unless it proves it took reasonable steps to ensure they would not contravene the Act -- for example by having an appropriate prevention policy in force and taking reasonable steps to implement and enforce it, including making staff aware of it and promptly investigating and acting on complaints.
GIVEN `was it done by their employee or agent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the act was done by an employee or agent of the person you ask about
      `was it in the course of the employment or agency` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was done while acting in the course of that employment or agency
      `have they proved reasonable steps to prevent it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they prove they took reasonable steps to ensure the employee or agent would not act in contravention of the Act
      `did they have a prevention policy in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they had an appropriate policy for preventing such acts in force at the time
      `did they take reasonable steps to implement and enforce it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they took reasonable steps to implement and enforce the policy
      `did they make staff aware of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they took reasonable steps to make their employees and agents aware of its terms
      `did they promptly investigate and act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they promptly investigated alleged acts and took appropriate action
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is the employer liable for its employee or agent` MEANS
    `s 91 -- they are vicariously liable` `was it done by their employee or agent` `was it in the course of the employment or agency` `have they proved reasonable steps to prevent it` `did they have a prevention policy in force` `did they take reasonable steps to implement and enforce it` `did they make staff aware of it` `did they promptly investigate and act`

@export Is the person who caused, instructed, induced or helped the unlawful act liable too (Equal Opportunity Act 1984 (SA) s 90)? Both that person and the one who did it are jointly and severally liable.
GIVEN `was there a contravention of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether someone acted in contravention of the Act (unlawful discrimination, sexual harassment or victimisation)
      `did this person cause, instruct, induce or aid it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person you ask about caused, instructed, induced or aided it
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is the person who helped liable too` MEANS
    `s 90 -- they are jointly and severally liable` `was there a contravention of the Act` `did this person cause, instruct, induce or aid it`

§§ `My complaint to the Commissioner`

@export By what day must I lodge my complaint with the Commissioner for Equal Opportunity (Equal Opportunity Act 1984 (SA) s 93(2))? Within 12 months of the act, or of the last act in a series of acts. The Commissioner may extend the time.
GIVEN `the day of the act` IS A DATE @desc The day of the act complained of or, for a series of acts, the day of the last of them
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I lodge my complaint` MEANS
    `s 93(2) -- the last day to lodge` `the day of the act`

@export Can the Commissioner extend my time to complain (Equal Opportunity Act 1984 (SA) s 93(2a))? On your application, even after the 12 months have run, if the Commissioner is satisfied there is a good reason the complaint was not made in time and that it is just and equitable to extend. Whether to extend is then the Commissioner's decision; a refusal must be notified in writing with your right of review.
GIVEN `have I applied for an extension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have applied to the Commissioner for an extension of time
      `is the Commissioner satisfied of a good reason` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner is satisfied there is a good reason why the complaint was not made in time
      `is the Commissioner satisfied it is just and equitable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner is satisfied that in all the circumstances it is just and equitable to extend
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the Commissioner extend my time` MEANS
    `s 93(2a) -- the Commissioner may extend the time` `have I applied for an extension` `is the Commissioner satisfied of a good reason` `is the Commissioner satisfied it is just and equitable`

@export Can I make this complaint to the Commissioner for Equal Opportunity (Equal Opportunity Act 1984 (SA) s 93(1)-(2a))? A person aggrieved may complain, for themselves or also for others aggrieved who consent in writing; for an aggrieved child or person with an intellectual disability, a representative the Commissioner thinks suitable. The complaint must be in writing with the details, lodged with the Commissioner within 12 months of the act (or the last of a series), unless the Commissioner extends the time.
GIVEN `who is complaining` IS A `Who complains` @desc Who makes the complaint. One of: "I, as a person aggrieved", "I, for myself and others aggrieved", "I, as representative of an aggrieved child or person with an intellectual disability", "someone who is none of these"
      `have the others consented in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a complaint on behalf of others: whether each of them consented in writing
      `does the Commissioner think me a suitable representative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a representative: whether the Commissioner considers you a suitable representative of the aggrieved person's interests
      `is it in writing with the details` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the complaint is in writing and sets out the details of the alleged contravention
      `is it lodged with the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is lodged with the Commissioner for Equal Opportunity
      `the day of the act complained of` IS A DATE @desc The day of the act complained of or, for a series of acts, the day of the last of them
      `the day I lodge it` IS A DATE @desc The day you lodge (or lodged) the complaint
      `has the Commissioner extended my time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has extended the time for lodging it
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I make the complaint` MEANS
    `s 93 -- the complaint may be made` `who is complaining` `have the others consented in writing` `does the Commissioner think me a suitable representative` `is it in writing with the details` `is it lodged with the Commissioner` (`s 93(2) -- my complaint is in time` `the day of the act complained of` `the day I lodge it` `has the Commissioner extended my time`)

@export Is my complaint lodged in time (Equal Opportunity Act 1984 (SA) s 93(2), (2a))? It is if lodged within 12 months of the act, or of the last of a series of acts, or if the Commissioner has extended the time.
GIVEN `the day of the act or last act` IS A DATE @desc The day of the act complained of or, for a series of acts, the day of the last of them
      `the day of lodging` IS A DATE @desc The day you lodge (or lodged) the complaint
      `did the Commissioner extend the time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has extended the time for lodging
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is my complaint in time` MEANS
    `s 93(2) -- my complaint is in time` `the day of the act or last act` `the day of lodging` `did the Commissioner extend the time`

@export By what day must I apply to the Tribunal to review the Commissioner's refusal to extend my time (Equal Opportunity Act 1984 (SA) s 96B(2))? Within 1 month after you were notified of the refusal.
GIVEN `the day I was told of the refusal` IS A DATE @desc The day you were notified of the Commissioner's refusal to extend time
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I apply for review of the refusal` MEANS
    `s 96B(2) -- the last day to apply for review` `the day I was told of the refusal`

@export Can I apply to the Tribunal (SACAT) to review the Commissioner's refusal to extend my time (Equal Opportunity Act 1984 (SA) s 96B)? Yes, under s 34 of the South Australian Civil and Administrative Tribunal Act 2013, within 1 month after notification of the refusal.
GIVEN `did the Commissioner refuse to extend` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner refused your application to extend the time for lodging the complaint
      `the day I was notified` IS A DATE @desc The day you were notified of the refusal
      `the day I apply to the Tribunal` IS A DATE @desc The day you apply (or applied) to the Tribunal for review
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I apply for review of the refusal` MEANS
    `s 96B -- I may apply for review of the refusal` `did the Commissioner refuse to extend` `the day I was notified` `the day I apply to the Tribunal`

@export Can the Commissioner deal with my complaint now (Equal Opportunity Act 1984 (SA) s 93(4))? Not while a criminal investigation of the matter is under way, or while a criminal charge about it is pending (until it is disposed of, withdrawn or permanently stayed).
GIVEN `is a criminal investigation under way` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a criminal investigation is being conducted into the matter you complain of
      `is a criminal charge pending` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether someone has been, or is to be, charged with a criminal offence over the matter and the charge has not been disposed of, withdrawn or permanently stayed
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the Commissioner deal with my complaint now` MEANS
    `s 93(4) -- the Commissioner may deal with my complaint now` `is a criminal investigation under way` `is a criminal charge pending`

§§ `After the complaint: declined, referred, heard`

@export Could the Commissioner decline to act on my complaint (Equal Opportunity Act 1984 (SA) s 95A(1), (4))? Only if, in the Commissioner's opinion, it is frivolous, vexatious, misconceived or lacking in substance; you have stopped pursuing it (died, cannot be contacted, said you will not go on or lost interest, or unreasonably refused to cooperate); there is no reasonable prospect of an order, or of one better than offers you refused in conciliation; or, for a complaint of domestic abuse discrimination, you gave no sufficient evidence of the abuse (an intervention order, help sought from a registered health practitioner, a charity or a prescribed body, or other evidence that satisfies the Commissioner).
GIVEN `does the Commissioner think it frivolous or lacking in substance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner considers the complaint frivolous, vexatious, misconceived or lacking in substance
      `does the Commissioner think I have stopped pursuing it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner considers you have died, cannot be contacted, said you will not proceed or shown a lack of interest, or unreasonably refused or failed to cooperate
      `does the Commissioner think there is no reasonable prospect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner considers there is no reasonable prospect of an order, or of one more favourable than offers you refused in conciliation
      `is my complaint of domestic abuse discrimination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the complaint alleges discrimination on the ground of being, or having been, subjected to domestic abuse
      `what evidence of the abuse did I give` IS A `My evidence of domestic abuse` @desc The evidence of domestic abuse you gave. One of: "an intervention order protecting me", "help I sought or received from a registered health practitioner", "help I sought or received from a charitable organisation", "help I sought or received from a prescribed person or body", "other evidence that satisfies the Commissioner", "none"
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Could the Commissioner decline my complaint` MEANS
    `s 95A(1) -- the Commissioner may decline my complaint` `does the Commissioner think it frivolous or lacking in substance` `does the Commissioner think I have stopped pursuing it` `does the Commissioner think there is no reasonable prospect` `is my complaint of domestic abuse discrimination` `what evidence of the abuse did I give`

@export Can the Commissioner reinstate my complaint after declining it because I stopped pursuing it (Equal Opportunity Act 1984 (SA) s 95A(3))? Yes, if you contact the Commissioner asking for it to proceed within 12 months after the date of that determination.
GIVEN `was it declined because I stopped pursuing it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner declined the complaint because you had died, could not be contacted, lost interest or would not cooperate (s 95A(1)(b))
      `the day of the Commissioner's determination` IS A DATE @desc The date of the Commissioner's determination
      `the day I asked to proceed` IS A DATE @desc The day you contact (or contacted) the Commissioner asking for the complaint to proceed
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can my declined complaint be reinstated` MEANS
    `s 95A(3) -- the Commissioner may reinstate my complaint` `was it declined because I stopped pursuing it` `the day of the Commissioner's determination` `the day I asked to proceed`

@export By what day must I require the Commissioner to refer my declined complaint to a tribunal (Equal Opportunity Act 1984 (SA) s 95B(1)(c))? Within 3 months of being notified of the Commissioner's decision to decline it, by notice in writing.
GIVEN `the day I was notified of the decline` IS A DATE @desc The day you were notified that the Commissioner declined to act on the complaint
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I require referral of my declined complaint` MEANS
    `s 95B(1)(c) -- the last day to require referral` `the day I was notified of the decline`

@export Must the Commissioner refer my complaint for hearing (Equal Opportunity Act 1984 (SA) s 95B(1))? The Commissioner must refer it if the Commissioner thinks it cannot be resolved by conciliation, conciliation has failed, or the Commissioner thinks it should be transferred; or, if the Commissioner declined it, if you required referral by written notice within 3 months of being notified.
GIVEN `where does my complaint stand` IS A `Where my complaint stands` @desc Where the complaint stands. One of: "the Commissioner thinks it cannot be resolved by conciliation", "conciliation was tried and failed", "the Commissioner thinks it should be transferred", "the Commissioner declined it", "it is still being dealt with or was resolved"
      `did I require referral in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a declined complaint: whether you required the Commissioner, by notice in writing, to refer it
      `the day I was notified it was declined` IS A DATE @desc For a declined complaint: the day you were notified of the decision
      `the day of my written notice` IS A DATE @desc For a declined complaint: the day of your written notice requiring referral
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must the Commissioner refer my complaint` MEANS
    `s 95B(1) -- the Commissioner must refer my complaint` `where does my complaint stand` `did I require referral in writing` `the day I was notified it was declined` `the day of my written notice`

@export Where will my complaint be heard if it is referred (Equal Opportunity Act 1984 (SA) s 95B(2), (2a))? Discrimination against a worker (any Part's Division 2), and victimisation, sexual harassment or assistance animal contraventions by someone you work with or sought to work with, go to the South Australian Employment Tribunal (SAET); everything else goes to the South Australian Civil and Administrative Tribunal; a complaint with both kinds may go to either, as the Commissioner thinks fit.
GIVEN `is it work discrimination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the complaint involves discrimination against a job applicant, employee, agent, contractor, contract worker or partner (Division 2 of Part 3, 4, 5, 5A or 5B)
      `is it victimisation, harassment or an assistance animal matter with a co-worker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it involves victimisation (s 86), sexual harassment (s 87) or separation from an assistance animal (s 88) by a person you work with, or were seeking to work with
      `does it involve other matters too` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it also involves other alleged contraventions (for example in goods and services, education or accommodation)
GIVETH A `Forum`
`Where will my complaint be heard` MEANS
    `s 95B(2), (2a) -- where my complaint is referred` `is it work discrimination` `is it victimisation, harassment or an assistance animal matter with a co-worker` `does it involve other matters too`

@export Can the Tribunal (or SAET) make this order for me (Equal Opportunity Act 1984 (SA) s 96)? Once it determines the respondent contravened the Act it may order compensation for loss or damage, including injury to feelings, in such amount as it thinks fit (no cap is set, but compensation awarded in other proceedings for the same acts is taken into account), an order to refrain from further contravention, or an order to perform specified acts to redress the loss or remedy the act; and it may make an interim order at any stage. No compensation may be awarded against a child (but it may be against someone vicariously liable for the child).
GIVEN `which order` IS AN `Order` @desc The order you seek. One of: "compensation, including for injury to feelings", "an order to refrain from further contravention", "an order to perform specified acts to redress the loss or remedy the act", "an interim order to prevent prejudice"
      `has it found a contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal or SAET has determined that the respondent acted in contravention of the Act
      `is the respondent a child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the respondent is under 18
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the tribunal make this order` MEANS
    `s 96 -- the tribunal may make the order` `which order` `has it found a contravention` `is the respondent a child`

@export Can I appeal to the Supreme Court (Equal Opportunity Act 1984 (SA) s 98A(1), (2))? A party may appeal against a decision or order of the Tribunal in proceedings on a complaint, or a decision on an application for an exemption. The appeal is a review of the decision.
GIVEN `which decision` IS A `The decision` @desc The decision. One of: "a decision or order in the proceedings on my complaint", "a decision on an application for an exemption", "another decision"
      `am I a party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were a party to the proceedings
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I appeal to the Supreme Court` MEANS
    `s 98A(1), (2) -- I may appeal to the Supreme Court` `which decision` `am I a party`

@export From what day does the time for my appeal run, if I asked for written reasons (Equal Opportunity Act 1984 (SA) s 98A(3)(b))? If the Tribunal did not give written reasons when it decided and you then asked for them, the time for appealing (set by s 71 of the South Australian Civil and Administrative Tribunal Act 2013) runs from when the written reasons are given to you. Otherwise that Act sets the start.
GIVEN `were written reasons given at the time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal gave its reasons in writing when it made the decision or order
      `did I then ask for written reasons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you then asked the Tribunal to state its reasons in writing
      `the day I received the written reasons` IS A DATE @desc The day the written statement of reasons was given to you
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`From when does my appeal time run` MEANS
    `s 98A(3)(b) -- the day my appeal time runs from` `were written reasons given at the time` `did I then ask for written reasons` `the day I received the written reasons`

§§ `Dismissal (only if you were dismissed): this Act or an unfair dismissal claim`

@export Does my unfair dismissal claim stop me bringing a discrimination claim about the dismissal (Equal Opportunity Act 1984 (SA) s 100(2), (3))? Once unfair dismissal proceedings (Fair Work Act 1994 (SA) Chapter 3 Part 6, or Fair Work Act 2009 (Cth) Part 3-2) about the dismissal are determined, you cannot bring or continue proceedings under this Act about it -- unless they were dismissed on a ground unrelated to a ground of discrimination under this Act.
GIVEN `did I bring unfair dismissal proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you brought unfair dismissal proceedings about this dismissal under the Fair Work Act 1994 (SA) or the Fair Work Act 2009 (Cth)
      `were they determined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether those proceedings have been determined
      `were they dismissed on an unrelated ground` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they were dismissed on a ground that does not relate to a ground of discrimination under this Act
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Am I barred from a discrimination claim about my dismissal` MEANS
    `s 100(2), (3) -- I am barred from proceedings under this Act` `did I bring unfair dismissal proceedings` `were they determined` `were they dismissed on an unrelated ground`

@export Does my discrimination claim stop me bringing a State unfair dismissal claim (Equal Opportunity Act 1984 (SA) s 100(4), (5))? Once proceedings under this Act about the dismissal are determined, you cannot bring or continue proceedings under the Fair Work Act 1994 (SA) about it -- unless the proceedings under this Act were dismissed and the unfair dismissal claim does not relate to a ground of discrimination. The section says nothing of a claim under the Fair Work Act 2009 (Cth).
GIVEN `did I bring proceedings under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you brought proceedings under the Equal Opportunity Act about the dismissal
      `have they been determined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether those proceedings have been determined
      `were they dismissed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether those proceedings were dismissed
      `does my unfair dismissal claim rest on discrimination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the unfair dismissal claim relates to a ground of discrimination under this Act
      `is my unfair dismissal claim a Commonwealth one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the unfair dismissal claim is under the Fair Work Act 2009 (Cth) rather than the Fair Work Act 1994 (SA)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Am I barred from an unfair dismissal claim` MEANS
    `s 100(4), (5) -- I am barred from an unfair dismissal claim` `did I bring proceedings under this Act` `have they been determined` `were they dismissed` `does my unfair dismissal claim rest on discrimination` `is my unfair dismissal claim a Commonwealth one`
